          "date": "2026-11-20 15:07:27.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-18687 lnet: iterate interface addresses with the kernel API",
        "message": "LU-18687 lnet: iterate interface addresses with the kernel API\n\nDECLARE_CONST_IN_IFADDR() and endfor_ifa() exist only in the\nlustre_compat inetdevice.h shim, so the callers do not build against\nthe kernel's own header.\n\nDeclare the cursor directly and drop endfor_ifa().  For kernels older\nthan v5.3, backfill in_dev_for_each_ifa_rtnl() and\nin_dev_for_each_ifa_rcu() as plain loops over ifa_list instead of\nmapping them to for_ifa().\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ieff2fd90144679d88b946ddeab5f65ce6a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
